WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.296
Human history,

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.090
is the story of one terrible

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.842
catastrophe after another.

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:12.095
I, for once, would love

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:14.223
to wake up magically
in a better world.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.184
Sylvie: What makes you think

00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:18.810
the world is going
to get better?

00:00:21.563 --> 00:00:24.024
Marshall: Today people get their
energy from the sun.

00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.903
Humans have set foot on Mars.

00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:30.030
Cancer has been defeated.

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.534
And yet, for every
question answered,

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:37.037
another one appears.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.874
Here's what you need to
know about global warming.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.168
It will all go to shit at
the end of the century.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:44.461
We'll be dead,

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:45.462
we'll have to miss it.

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:47.839
But we'll be smiling in
gold plated coffins.

00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:50.884
This is not the life

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:51.927
that I envisioned it to be.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.347
The man whose house is on fire

00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:57.224
is incredibly easy
to negotiate with.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:02.479
We cannot give up and go home.

00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:05.816
For one simple reason.

00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.902
We already are home.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.321
This is our only home.

00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:15.617
I think it helps to look at
climate change like a bear.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:18.829
The whole planet's
been wrestling

00:01:18.829 --> 00:01:20.080
with the bear for decades.

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:24.251
So far, the bear's
been kicking our ass.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:26.795
Nick: What if we were able

00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:30.215
to develop technology that
would allow us to survive,

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:31.800
maybe even thrive?

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:33.969
Jonathan: You don't know what's
going to happen.

00:01:35.262 --> 00:01:36.513
Olivia: It won't go the way you want.

00:01:38.265 --> 00:01:39.099
It never does.

00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:42.477
Erza: I remember being happy.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:43.645
Daddy!

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:44.646
What about now?

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:46.940
Natasha: Are you happy now?

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:49.818
Are we bad people?

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.946
Stop being angry about the past.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.990
The future is now.

00:01:55.574 --> 00:01:58.577
♪♪

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.750
Miami is dangerous.

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.377
Your mother's moving with
her sister in Chicago.

00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:08.754
Thought you hated your sister?

00:02:08.754 --> 00:02:11.131
It's too hot out,

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.675
to hate people
these days Marshall.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:20.140
♪♪

